(text "HEEL SWITCH" (at 55.88 199.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid c74ed5ee-4adf-4d2c-b598-4f7e3a16c36e))
(text "SWITCHES (internal pull-ups)" (at 170.18 218.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1da48bf1-1872-4e02-85c3-623fa221f6b1))
(text "OPERATOR INPUTS (RC-filtered ADC)" (at 20.32 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid f9f14972-9ac2-4c82-a9ae-9e144058f400))
(text "NOTES. A concept drawn by Claude at Bob Drzyzgula's direction, October 2026: not built, not tested, values not checked." (at 20.32 258.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid e63d4ab1-e48f-4ac6-9574-77658798977e))
(text "1. After Freescale AN1662: zero-cross interrupt sets a timer alarm (or a PIO program); at the firing delay a ~100 us gate pulse fires the" (at 20.32 261.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9886a31f-7217-4aa7-b7c5-4f3bad85243d))
(text "   triac; hand-wheel period from edge timestamps; speed loop every half-cycle (120 Hz); stall watchdog. Added: isolation, relay, inputs." (at 20.32 263.40000000000003 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 734280ae-529b-4c0f-ac3a-f0ea7f372328))
(text "2. Pins (RP2350B): FIRE GP4; RELAY GP5; ZC GP6; HALL (index) GP7; ENC_A/B GP2/GP3 (PIO counter); STITCH GP10; HEEL GP11; NEEDLE GP12;" (at 20.32 265.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid b016f509-3abc-445b-aa6f-da5857a24285))
(text "   knee, pedal, FSR, limit on ADC0-3 (GP40-43); ISENSE ADC4; ADC5-7 spare; GP8/GP9 UART1 for debug (or USB serial). Avoid GP0, GP23, GP25 (PSRAM, key, LED)." (at 20.32 268.20000000000005 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5b34abd9-30e6-48fa-8805-99dcdc2e8962))
(text "3. PS1 feeds VSYS through D2, so USB may stay plugged in (the control side is SELV). Flash by UF2 (BOOTSEL) or SWD. Drive GP4 at 8-12 mA." (at 20.32 270.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2d953d00-9841-4629-afdb-96462a698e36))
(text "4. Fire only after a zero-cross has been seen and the command is zero; close K1 last and open it first. Never scope the line side." (at 20.32 273.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9e3b4e95-c909-4dae-8754-f316acdfdf8a))
(text "5. R7/R8: ~3.9 mA peak in the H11AA1; R11: ~8 mA into U3 from 3.3 V; R6/C2 fitted only if a snubberless triac false-fires. T1 optional: the bridge's AC lead through its window, 0.1 V/A about 1.65 V." (at 20.32 275.40000000000003 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bddd2b01-dfe2-4fc1-b8d6-90b18938722b))
(text "6. On a WeAct RP2350B Core board, feed PS1 to the 5V pin: the board has its own diode from USB VBUS, so D2 may be left out." (at 20.32 277.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 0e6dc9e1-7f04-4aec-9bc0-631cec8f11cd))
(text "7. Heel: momentary switch to GND in either pedal (J5 pin 4, J6 pin 3); a heel tap sends the needle to its other stop." (at 20.32 280.20000000000005 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 8428efca-dcbe-43e2-81f0-f7228b346e45))
(text "8. Encoder U5/U6 (ring of alternating magnets) optional: stops taught and landed by angle; 5-wire cable (3V3, GND, index, A, B)." (at 20.32 282.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3850048c-0e97-4f22-b62e-d90c57b18fe7))
(text "9. RECTIFIED-DC VARIANT: BR1 turns the triac's output into DC; D3 carries the motor's current between firings. J3 is the motor's own keyed" (at 20.32 285.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid b537b299-fc97-49f1-807a-edd640e05b85))
(text "   connector (or the leads pass through and are hardwired), never a mains outlet, and is at line potential. T1 sits on the AC side: a CT can't sense DC." (at 20.32 287.40000000000003 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 98b88d43-338a-420f-8492-43b90bbd259f))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))))
